The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) treated the merged ticket as one parser bug.
The export supports separate parser and booking-form investigations, plus unresolved timing reports.
Use [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-evidence) and the
[current triage procedure](/kb/triage/dedupe) for incoming reports.

<Callout kind="warn">
The export contains support reports and classification code, not the production parser or form.
The model helps route investigation. Production reproductions and fixes remain unverified.
</Callout>

<InvestigationTable ticket={4471} />

## Representative evidence

- R-41200, Harbour Dental app: a reminder for 7 April went out on 4 July. R-41203, Lantern Row app: 2 December became 12 February. These bodies support a month/day swap investigation.
- R-41205, Morrow Tax app: tenant locale is fr-FR, although browser locale is en-US and intake guessed hint. Tenant configuration puts it on the parser path.
- R-41230, Copper Studio form: intake guessed parser. Its day-first tenant uses booking-v3, so the export routes it to the hint group. R-41241, Alder Physio form, describes 6 August becoming 8 June.
- R-41236 says an invite arrived before the booking was made. It is weaker evidence of a one-day shift and may need a separate delivery-order investigation.

The raw report bodies, intake metadata and tenant directory remain in `src/lib/data`.
The original `causes.ts` model remains unchanged. `investigation.ts` deduplicates IDs and
holds the desk-noted exceptions apart, without inventing a root cause.

## Backlog versus new inflow

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The chart counts each report ID once. The received series uses `receivedAt`; the merged series uses
`mergedAt`. Reports arrived from April onward, while early July merges included reports received
months earlier. A burst of merges can be backlog processing. It does not establish a burst of new
failures or an overnight change in the report count. Compare arrivals with merges before escalating
a new-inflow claim. The timeline also cannot prove when the underlying production bug began.

## Follow-up work

Investigate the shared month-first parser separately from the booking-v3 date hint. Keep the timing
exceptions open pending timestamps, timezone offsets, calendar payloads and delivery logs.
The approved issue drafts are `docs/issues/parser-ticket.md`, `docs/issues/hint-ticket.md` and
`docs/issues/one-day-ticket.md` at the repository root.

